{"schema":"learning-v2-theory.v1","lesson":6,"lang":"pl","title":"Co ludzie robią","sections":[{"num":"01","title":"Czego się nauczysz","defaultOpen":true,"blocks":[{"kind":"body","text":"Do tej pory zdania mówiły, jaki ktoś jest i gdzie: I am ready, it is here. Teraz będą o tym, co ludzie robią: «pracuję w aptece», «kosimy trawnik», «on jeździ do pracy samochodem». To rzeczy, które się powtarzają: praca, nawyki, plan dnia."},{"kind":"examples","examples":[{"en":"I work in a pharmacy.","translation":"Pracuję w aptece.","hi":"work"},{"en":"We mow the lawn.","translation":"Kosimy trawnik.","hi":"mow"},{"en":"He drives to work.","translation":"Jeździ do pracy samochodem.","hi":"drives"},{"en":"She teaches English.","translation":"Uczy angielskiego.","hi":"teaches"}]}]},{"num":"02","title":"Kto + czynność","defaultOpen":true,"blocks":[{"kind":"body","text":"Po polsku «pracuję» już mówi, że to ja. Po angielsku trzeba powiedzieć, kto: I work. A między kto i czynnością nie stoi am, is ani are: I am work to błąd."},{"kind":"formula","formula":[{"text":"kto","accent":true},{"text":"czynność","accent":false},{"text":"co / gdzie / kiedy","accent":true}]},{"kind":"examples","examples":[{"en":"I work in a pharmacy.","translation":"Pracuję w aptece.","hi":"work"},{"en":"I bake bread.","translation":"Piekę chleb.","hi":"bake"},{"en":"You sweep the floor.","translation":"Zamiatasz podłogę.","hi":"sweep"},{"en":"We trim the hedge.","translation":"Przycinamy żywopłot.","hi":"trim"},{"en":"They build a wall.","translation":"Budują mur.","hi":"build"}]},{"kind":"fix","fixes":[{"wrong":"Work in a pharmacy.","right":"I work in a pharmacy."},{"wrong":"I am work in a pharmacy.","right":"I work in a pharmacy."}]},{"kind":"drill","drill":{"type":"binary","kind":"binary","question":"Mówisz, gdzie pracujesz. Które zdanie jest poprawne?","optionA":"Work in a pharmacy.","optionB":"I work in a pharmacy.","correct":"B","explain":"Po angielsku trzeba powiedzieć I na początku."}}]},{"num":"03","title":"I, you, we, they — czynność jak w słowniku","defaultOpen":false,"blocks":[{"kind":"body","text":"Po polsku każda osoba ma swoją końcówkę: pracuję, pracujemy, pracują. Po angielsku z I, you, we i they czynność się nie zmienia: work, wash, carry. To łatwiejsze."},{"kind":"examples","examples":[{"en":"I wash the plates.","translation":"Myję talerze.","hi":"wash"},{"en":"You carry the trays.","translation":"Nosisz tace.","hi":"carry"},{"en":"We pick pears.","translation":"Zbieramy gruszki.","hi":"pick"},{"en":"They dig in the yard.","translation":"Kopią na podwórku.","hi":"dig"},{"en":"We play football in the yard.","translation":"Gramy w piłkę na podwórku.","hi":"play"},{"en":"I ride a bicycle.","translation":"Jeżdżę na rowerze.","hi":"ride"}]},{"kind":"fix","fixes":[{"wrong":"We picks pears.","right":"We pick pears."},{"wrong":"They digs in the yard.","right":"They dig in the yard."}]}]},{"num":"04","title":"He, she, it — na końcu pojawia się s","defaultOpen":false,"blocks":[{"kind":"body","text":"Z he, she, it albo z jedną osobą — the host, my brother — czynność dostaje s: he drives, she waits, the host greets. To jedyna zmiana i dlatego łatwo o niej zapomnieć: He drive to najczęstszy błąd lekcji."},{"kind":"formula","formula":[{"text":"he / she / it / jedna osoba","accent":true},{"text":"czynność + s","accent":false}]},{"kind":"examples","examples":[{"en":"He drives to work.","translation":"Jeździ do pracy samochodem.","hi":"drives"},{"en":"She waits at the bus stop.","translation":"Czeka na przystanku.","hi":"waits"},{"en":"She smiles at the baby.","translation":"Uśmiecha się do dziecka.","hi":"smiles"},{"en":"He tastes the soup.","translation":"Próbuje zupy.","hi":"tastes"},{"en":"The host greets the guests.","translation":"Gospodarz wita gości.","hi":"greets"},{"en":"It sleeps on the quilt.","translation":"Śpi na kołdrze. *(kot)*","hi":"sleeps"}]},{"kind":"fix","fixes":[{"wrong":"He drive to work.","right":"He drives to work."},{"wrong":"Drives to work.","right":"He drives to work."},{"wrong":"I works in a pharmacy.","right":"I work in a pharmacy."}]},{"kind":"drill","drill":{"type":"choice","kind":"choice","before":"She","after":"at the bus stop.","options":["wait","waits","is wait"],"answer":"waits","why":"Z she czynność dostaje s."}}]},{"num":"05","title":"Kiedy potrzebne jest es","defaultOpen":false,"blocks":[{"kind":"body","text":"Jeśli czynność kończy się na sh, ch, s albo x, samego s nie da się wymówić: dodaje się es i pojawia się sylaba. wash → washes, catch → catches, teach → teaches, fish → fishes, mix → mixes."},{"kind":"examples","examples":[{"en":"She teaches English.","translation":"Uczy angielskiego.","hi":"teaches"},{"en":"She catches the bus.","translation":"Zdąża na autobus.","hi":"catches"},{"en":"He fishes with a rod.","translation":"Łowi ryby na wędkę.","hi":"fishes"},{"en":"She washes the saucers.","translation":"Myje spodeczki.","hi":"washes"}]},{"kind":"fix","fixes":[{"wrong":"She teachs English.","right":"She teaches English."},{"wrong":"He fishs with a rod.","right":"He fishes with a rod."}]}]},{"num":"06","title":"Kiedy y zmienia się w ies","defaultOpen":false,"blocks":[{"kind":"body","text":"Jeśli czynność kończy się na y, a przed nim stoi spółgłoska, y zmienia się w ies: study → studies, carry → carries. Jeśli przed y jest samogłoska, wystarczy s: play → plays."},{"kind":"examples","examples":[{"en":"She studies with a tutor.","translation":"Uczy się z korepetytorem.","hi":"studies"},{"en":"My brother carries a bundle.","translation":"Brat niesie pakunek.","hi":"carries"},{"en":"He plays football.","translation":"Gra w piłkę.","hi":"plays"}]},{"kind":"fix","fixes":[{"wrong":"She studys with a tutor.","right":"She studies with a tutor."},{"wrong":"He plaies football.","right":"He plays football."}]},{"kind":"drill","drill":{"type":"choice","kind":"choice","before":"She","after":"with a tutor.","options":["studys","studies","study"],"answer":"studies","why":"Przed y stoi spółgłoska d, więc y zmienia się w ies."}}]},{"num":"07","title":"To o tym, co dzieje się regularnie","defaultOpen":false,"blocks":[{"kind":"body","text":"Takie zdania mówią o pracy, nawykach i tym, co się powtarza: I walk to work — «chodzę do pracy pieszo» (zwykle, codziennie). Nie mówią o tym, co dzieje się właśnie teraz, w tej sekundzie."},{"kind":"examples","examples":[{"en":"I walk to work.","translation":"Chodzę do pracy pieszo.","hi":"walk"},{"en":"I cycle to work.","translation":"Jeżdżę do pracy rowerem.","hi":"cycle"},{"en":"I exercise at home.","translation":"Ćwiczę w domu.","hi":"exercise"},{"en":"She lives in a flat.","translation":"Mieszka w mieszkaniu.","hi":"lives"},{"en":"They sell lamps.","translation":"Sprzedają lampy.","hi":"sell"}]}]},{"num":"08","title":"Gdzie i kiedy — na końcu","defaultOpen":false,"blocks":[{"kind":"body","text":"Gdzie i kiedy zwykle stawia się na końcu: I start at two — «zaczynam o drugiej», She reads in the armchair — «czyta w fotelu». Godzina idzie z at: at two, at five. Polskie «o» to tu at, a nie on ani in."},{"kind":"examples","examples":[{"en":"I start at two.","translation":"Zaczynam o drugiej.","hi":"at"},{"en":"I arrive at five.","translation":"Przyjeżdżam o piątej.","hi":"at"},{"en":"She leaves at four.","translation":"Wychodzi o czwartej.","hi":"at"},{"en":"She reads in the armchair.","translation":"Czyta w fotelu.","hi":"in"},{"en":"We jog at sunrise.","translation":"Biegamy o wschodzie słońca.","hi":"at"}]},{"kind":"fix","fixes":[{"wrong":"I start on two.","right":"I start at two."},{"wrong":"At two I start.","right":"I start at two."}]}]},{"num":"09","title":"Czynność albo is — nie oba naraz","defaultOpen":false,"blocks":[{"kind":"body","text":"Jeśli jest czynność, nie ma am, is, are: She cooks. Jeśli czynności nie ma, a mówisz, kim ktoś jest albo jaki jest — is potrzebne, razem z kto: She is an artist. Oba naraz nie: She is cooks to błąd."},{"kind":"examples","examples":[{"en":"She is an artist.","translation":"Jest malarką.","hi":"is"},{"en":"This artist paints portraits.","translation":"Ten artysta maluje portrety.","hi":"paints"},{"en":"He is a baker.","translation":"Jest piekarzem.","hi":"is"},{"en":"The tailor repairs uniforms.","translation":"Krawiec naprawia mundury.","hi":"repairs"},{"en":"I am a beginner.","translation":"Jestem początkujący.","hi":"am"}]},{"kind":"fix","fixes":[{"wrong":"She is cooks at home.","right":"She cooks at home."},{"wrong":"Is baker.","right":"He is a baker."}]},{"kind":"drill","drill":{"type":"word_bank","kind":"word_bank","prompt":"Powiedz: «Krawiec naprawia mundury».","answer":["The","tailor","repairs","uniforms"],"distractors":["is","repair"]}}]},{"num":"10","title":"Błędy, które robi prawie każdy","defaultOpen":false,"blocks":[{"kind":"fix","fixes":[{"wrong":"Work in a pharmacy.","right":"I work in a pharmacy."},{"wrong":"He drive to work.","right":"He drives to work."},{"wrong":"I works at home.","right":"I work at home."},{"wrong":"She teachs English.","right":"She teaches English."},{"wrong":"She studys with a tutor.","right":"She studies with a tutor."},{"wrong":"She is cooks at home.","right":"She cooks at home."},{"wrong":"I start on two.","right":"I start at two."}]},{"kind":"tip","text":"Trzy sprawdzenia. Powiedziałeś, kto? Jest czynność — bez am, is, are. To he, she, it albo jedna osoba — dodaj s."}]},{"num":"11","title":"Co zabrać do ćwiczeń","defaultOpen":false,"blocks":[{"kind":"body","text":"Kto + czynność, zawsze z kto i bez is. I, you, we, they — czynność jak w słowniku. He, she, it — plus s, czasem es albo ies. Gdzie i kiedy na końcu, godzina z at."},{"kind":"examples","examples":[{"en":"We pack the bags.","translation":"Pakujemy torby.","hi":"pack"},{"en":"He coughs.","translation":"Kaszle.","hi":"coughs"},{"en":"She catches the bus.","translation":"Zdąża na autobus.","hi":"catches"},{"en":"She studies with a tutor.","translation":"Uczy się z korepetytorem.","hi":"studies"},{"en":"I arrive at five.","translation":"Przyjeżdżam o piątej.","hi":"arrive"}]}]}],"sessionSection":{}}
